# CaesarIA - iOS and iPadOS Installation Guide

This guide will help you build and install CaesarIA for iOS (iPhone) and iPadOS (iPad).

## Requirements

- macOS (required for iOS development)
- Xcode 13.0 or later (available from Mac App Store)
- Xcode Command Line Tools
- CMake 3.14 or later
- Original Caesar III game resources (.sg2, .555 files)

## Installing Prerequisites

### 1. Install Xcode
Download and install Xcode from the Mac App Store.

### 2. Install Command Line Tools
```bash
xcode-select --install
```

### 3. Install CMake
Using Homebrew (recommended):
```bash
brew install cmake
```

Or download from: https://cmake.org/download/

## Building for iOS Device (iPhone/iPad)

### 1. Clone the repository
```bash
git clone https://github.com/dalerank/caesaria-game.git
cd caesaria-game
```

### 2. Create build directory
```bash
mkdir build-ios
cd build-ios
```

### 3. Configure with CMake for iOS
```bash
cmake .. \
  -G Xcode \
  -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=../cmake/Modules/ios.toolchain.cmake \
  -DPLATFORM=OS \
  -DDEPLOYMENT_TARGET=13.0 \
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release
```

### 4. Build the project
```bash
cmake --build . --config Release
```

Alternatively, open the generated Xcode project:
```bash
open CaesarIA.xcodeproj
```

## Building for iOS Simulator

For testing on the iOS Simulator:

```bash
mkdir build-ios-simulator
cd build-ios-simulator

cmake .. \
  -G Xcode \
  -DCMAKE_TOOLCHAIN_FILE=../cmake/Modules/ios.toolchain.cmake \
  -DPLATFORM=SIMULATOR \
  -DDEPLOYMENT_TARGET=13.0 \
  -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release

cmake --build . --config Release
```

## Installing Resources

CaesarIA requires original Caesar III resources to run.

### 1. Prepare resources
Copy your Caesar III resources to the `resources/gfx` folder:
- .sg2 files (graphics)
- .555 files (graphics)
- .smk files to `resources/smk` (videos)
- .wav files to `resources/audio` (sounds)

### 2. Bundle resources with app
The build process will automatically include resources in the app bundle.

## Installing on Device

### Option 1: Using Xcode (Recommended for testing)

1. Connect your iPhone or iPad via USB
2. Open the Xcode project: `build-ios/CaesarIA.xcodeproj`
3. Select your device from the device menu
4. Click the "Run" button (or press Cmd+R)

Note: You'll need to configure code signing in Xcode:
- Select the project in Xcode
- Go to "Signing & Capabilities"
- Select your development team
- Xcode will automatically create provisioning profiles

### Option 2: TestFlight (For distribution)

1. Archive the app in Xcode: Product → Archive
2. Upload to App Store Connect
3. Distribute via TestFlight to testers

### Option 3: Ad-Hoc Distribution

1. Archive the app in Xcode
2. Export with "Ad Hoc" distribution
3. Install via Apple Configurator or Xcode Devices window

## Touch Controls

CaesarIA includes enhanced touch controls for iOS/iPadOS:

- **Tap**: Select buildings, units, or UI elements
- **Double-tap**: Quick access to building information
- **Drag**: Scroll the map
- **Pinch**: Zoom in/out (if enabled)
- **Two-finger tap**: Context menu (equivalent to right-click)
- **Long press**: Additional options/information

## Troubleshooting

### Code Signing Issues
If you encounter code signing errors:
1. Open Xcode
2. Go to Preferences → Accounts
3. Add your Apple ID
4. Download manual profiles if needed

### Missing SDK
If CMake can't find the iOS SDK:
```bash
xcode-select --print-path
sudo xcode-select --switch /Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer
```

### Build Errors
Make sure you have the latest Xcode:
```bash
softwareupdate --list
softwareupdate --install "Xcode"
```

## Performance Tips

- iOS devices work best with medium-to-high graphics settings
- iPad Pro models can handle maximum settings at 60 FPS
- Older devices (iPhone 8 or earlier) may benefit from reduced graphics quality
- Enable "Reduce Animations" in settings for better performance

